---
layout: changelog
title: "Old deployments will no longer fill up your Appwrite Cloud storage"
date: 2026-10-21
cover: /images/blog/default-deployment-retention/cover.avif
description: "From November 5, 2026, inactive deployments on Appwrite Cloud are cleaned up after 30 days by default, which frees up storage on every plan."
tags: functions, sites, storage
---

Every deployment of a function or site counts toward your storage, even after a newer one replaces it. From **November 5, 2026**, inactive deployments on Appwrite Cloud are cleaned up automatically once they're more than **30 days** old, and the space goes back to your files and databases. On the Free plan, that can free up a big part of your 2GB of storage. Your active deployment and any deployment a custom domain points to always stay.

**Keep deployments forever**, today's default, switches to 30 days on November 5. To keep more history, set a retention period in your function or site's **Settings** > **Build** > **Retention** before then: up to **90 days** and the **100** newest inactive deployments on the Free and Education plans, or up to **3 years** on the Start and Pro plans. Self-hosted Appwrite is unchanged.

